    shortAnswer: 'Conway\'s Law predicts architecture mirrors communication structure — if one team owns both sides of a proposed split, there is no organizational seam for the service boundary to relieve. The team pays the full cost (network calls, two deploy pipelines, two on-call surfaces) while gaining no team-autonomy benefit, since the same people already coordinate freely within themselves.',
