    shortAnswer: "Both avoid recomputing the aggregate on every read, but the failure mode differs: a denormalized counter (updated in the write path or via an event) can silently drift out of sync if any write path forgets to update it, while a materialized view's staleness is explicit and bounded by its refresh schedule — you know exactly how stale it is, rather than discovering a bug in sync logic.",
