    shortAnswer: 'Every event already persisted under the old name still has the old field, and any future replay (rebuild, new consumer bootstrapping, DR restore) deserializes those old records — a straight rename breaks deserialization or silently drops the old data for everything before the change. Safe evolution means either adding the new field alongside the old one and dual-writing/dual-reading during a transition, or introducing a new event version with an explicit upcaster that translates old-shaped events into the new shape at read time, and only retiring the old field once every consumer has migrated.',
