    detailedAnswer: "Diagrams tend to show redundancy at the layer people think about most (app servers, databases) and silently omit the layers everyone assumes 'just work' — DNS, certificate authorities, identity/secrets management, and third-party dependencies. A practical SPOF audit walks every component and asks 'what does this depend on that isn't itself redundant across the same failure domain?' Common finds: all 'redundant' AZs still route through one region-wide load balancer config; all services depend on one central secrets manager with no regional failover; the only path to deploy a fix during an incident runs through a single CI/CD system that itself has no DR plan.",
