    question: "What's the practical difference between client-side and server-side service discovery, and which does a typical Kubernetes deployment use?",
    shortAnswer: "Client-side discovery has the caller query the registry directly and pick + balance across instances itself (e.g. Netflix Eureka + Ribbon); server-side discovery has the caller hit a stable address and an intermediary (load balancer/gateway) does the registry lookup and routing. Kubernetes uses server-side discovery — pods call a Service's stable ClusterIP and kube-proxy routes to a healthy pod, so application code never talks to the underlying registry.",
